00:15:12.370 --> 00:15:13.795
that it can handle, I guess?

00:15:13.795 --> 00:15:16.420
You were saying you could use it
as a document DB if you really

00:15:16.420 --> 00:15:16.550
want.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:17.570
LUCIA SUBATIN: Yeah,
on top of that,

00:15:17.570 --> 00:15:19.413
you can do text mining
and text analytics.

00:15:19.413 --> 00:15:20.080
MARK MANDEL: OK.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:21.680
LUCIA SUBATIN: And there
are some combination.

00:15:21.680 --> 00:15:23.380
Then you have the
combination of that.

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.507
We have streaming
analytics, like for IoT.

00:15:25.507 --> 00:15:27.340
And that is something
I actually implemented

00:15:27.340 --> 00:15:29.260
in my city of birth.

00:15:29.260 --> 00:15:31.960
So you get information
coming from sensors,

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:34.720
and you can run predictive, and
you can run certain algorithms

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:38.590
while the information is
getting pumped into the database

00:15:38.590 --> 00:15:39.350
as well.

00:15:39.350 --> 00:15:42.040
So that is also another
cool feature that it has.

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:44.530
And one thing that
people ask me a lot

00:15:44.530 --> 00:15:47.470
is if it's an in-memory
database, which

00:15:47.470 --> 00:15:50.020
makes it very fast,
what happens to the data

00:15:50.020 --> 00:15:51.040
if the light goes off?

00:15:51.040 --> 00:15:54.850
And I can assure you that
the data is stored in disk.

00:15:54.850 --> 00:15:55.607
MARK MANDEL: OK.

00:15:55.607 --> 00:15:57.190
LUCIA SUBATIN: So
you were saying SSD.

00:15:57.190 --> 00:16:00.070
Logically, yes, data
is stored in disk.

00:16:00.070 --> 00:16:02.260
One thing about the
architecture of HANA

00:16:02.260 --> 00:16:05.170
and why it was
thought this way is

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:07.000
not only the
in-memory capabilities

00:16:07.000 --> 00:16:09.190
and the processing
happened in RAM,

00:16:09.190 --> 00:16:11.860
it also happens
in the CPU cache.

00:16:11.860 --> 00:16:14.290
So it's extremely fast.

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:17.980
And by being columnar and
combining this architecture,

00:16:17.980 --> 00:16:21.010
you can get rid
of materialization

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:24.040
of data or copies of
data inside the database.

00:16:24.040 --> 00:16:26.390
And by that, I also mean
[INAUDIBLE] for example.

00:16:26.390 --> 00:16:30.220
So they are not as necessary
as in a traditional database.

00:16:30.220 --> 00:16:35.080
And we found in internal
studies that once you migrate,

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:40.390
you get rate of 60% to 95%
of the objects in a database

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.542
because you do not need
the redundancy anymore.

00:16:42.542 --> 00:16:43.750
MARK MANDEL: Oh, interesting.

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.880
LUCIA SUBATIN: So that's
another long answer

00:16:45.880 --> 00:16:48.190
to this type of
capability, but it's

00:16:48.190 --> 00:16:51.850
one of the reasons why we
are shifting our applications

00:16:51.850 --> 00:16:53.133
towards HANA as well.

00:16:53.133 --> 00:16:54.550
MARK MANDEL: So
if I'm a developer

00:16:54.550 --> 00:16:56.140
and I'm like, this
sounds really cool,

00:16:56.140 --> 00:16:57.640
how do I build on
top of SAP HANA?

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:59.698
Do I need to be part
of the SAP ecosystem?

00:16:59.698 --> 00:17:01.990
Or can I just pick a programming
language and go at it?

00:17:01.990 --> 00:17:03.310
Or how does that work?

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:04.990
LUCIA SUBATIN: You can pick
up any programming language

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:07.599
and go at it, as long as you can
connect through JDBC or ODBC.

00:17:07.599 --> 00:17:08.619
MARK MANDEL: Oh, nice.

00:17:08.619 --> 00:17:10.760
LUCIA SUBATIN: That's like
with any other database.

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.180
We also have an
application layer

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:15.099
that is based on Cloud Foundry.

00:17:15.099 --> 00:17:19.000
So if you want to build
microservices based,

00:17:19.000 --> 00:17:21.430
we officially support
free build packs.

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.950
And we have a lot of libraries
to connect and to enhance

00:17:23.950 --> 00:17:26.950
that for Java,
JavaScript, and Python.

00:17:26.950 --> 00:17:28.990
So that's another option
if you are into it.

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:29.980
And then it's just SQL.

00:17:29.980 --> 00:17:31.870
All these capabilities
that I mentioned,

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:33.700
they're all SQL based.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:36.040
So you do not need
to learn a lot.

00:17:36.040 --> 00:17:37.870
And if you want to
deploy it, I have

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:39.460
to say that my
favorite options-- we

00:17:39.460 --> 00:17:41.800
have a lot of options to
deploy HANA, specifically

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:42.475
HANA Express.

